{
  "schemaVersion": 19,
  "description": "Timetables on a line a(0,1)-b(1,1)-c(2,1)-d(3,1)-e(4,1) with dead ends at both ends. Alpha(1,0) has platform b, Beta(3,0) has platform d, and Gamma(5,2) has no platform. A timetable is a train's ordered list of stops, each a station with a scheduled arrival and departure in game minutes since the start (the clock's scale). setTrainTimetable replaces the whole list and [] clears it; it is free and the train may be unplaced. Times must never go back from minute 0: 0 <= arrival <= departure at every stop, and each departure <= the next arrival; equal times, repeated stations, stations without platforms and times the clock has passed are allowed. Checks, in the order unknownTrain, invalidTimetable, unknownStation (the first missing station in timetable order): new trains have none (also after another train got one), one-stop and multi-stop timetables, zero dwell and equal boundaries, replacing and clearing, rejected commands leave the timetable as it was; the timetable survives place, rate, continuation, advance, reverse, unplace and a second place, and setting one keeps the train's continuation and rate; and it is inert: it never places, moves, routes or stops a train, a train stopped at a scheduled station stays there after its departure time has passed, and time passing every scheduled minute leaves the timetable as it was.",
